 byte-based values crashed it with "charIndex out of range" on non-ASCII
 sources — M8 fuzzer find, fixed).
 
+Synthesized nodes have no source position (`token.NoPos`): the exporter emits
+a defined synthetic position instead of arithmetic on it (R-1107-04). A node
+with no valid start carries `{ "file": 0, "line": 1, "col": 1, "off": 0,
+"len": 0 }`; a node with a valid start but no usable end (end missing, before
+the start, or in a different file — e.g. a disk-MR `__`-helper's synthetic
+`FuncType`, whose start falls through to the shared original params while its
+end falls through to a synthetic ident) carries a zero-length section at its
+real start. Every emitted `pos` therefore satisfies `line >= 1` and
+`len >= 0`, which `tools/validate_frontend_v1.py` (`check_pos`) enforces.
+
